<h3>3.2 CPS Detail Flat File — BIL* Lines (rfrBillDelimitedLineTokenizer &amp; RfrDetailFieldSetMapper.java)</h3>
<p>- <b>Delimiter</b>: Semicolon (<code>;</code>)</p>
<p>- <b>Total Columns in File</b>: <code>66</code> (<code>0</code> through <code>65</code>)</p>
<p>- **Active Columns for <code>BIL*</code> Lines**: Columns <code>0</code> through <code>42</code> (<code>43</code> fields mapped when <code>lineType</code> starts with <code>&quot;BIL&quot;</code>, e.g., <code>&quot;BILA&quot;</code>, <code>&quot;BILB&quot;</code>). If <code>lineType</code> does not start with <code>&quot;BIL&quot;</code>, <code>RfrDetailBisToDbProcessor</code> returns <code>null</code> (skips the line).</p>
<table>
<tr>
<th>Col Index</th>
<th>Tokenizer Field Name</th>
<th>Java Field (<code>RfrDetail.java</code>)</th>
<th>Data Type</th>
<th>Mapping / Parsing Rule</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>0</code></td>
<td><code>lineType</code></td>
<td><code>lineType</code> / <code>alphabetKey</code></td>
<td><code>String</code> / <code>char</code></td>
<td>Must start with <code>&quot;BIL&quot;</code>. <code>alphabetKey = lineType.charAt(3)</code> (e.g. <code>&apos;A&apos;</code> from <code>&quot;BILA&quot;</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>1</code></td>
<td><code>serviceStartDate</code></td>
<td><code>serviceStartDate</code></td>
<td><code>Date</code></td>
<td>Parsed as <code>yyyy-MM-dd</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>2</code></td>
<td><code>serviceEndDate</code></td>
<td><code>serviceEndDate</code></td>
<td><code>Date</code></td>
<td>Parsed as <code>yyyy-MM-dd</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>3</code></td>
<td><code>payCode</code></td>
<td><code>payCode</code></td>
<td><code>String</code></td>
<td>Payment code (<code>HOSP</code>, <code>DRLB</code>, <code>REHA</code>, <code>RXSP</code>, <code>ACAG</code>, <code>RESI</code>, <code>EQUP</code>, <code>PROS</code>, <code>TRAN</code>, <code>CSMT</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>4</code></td>
<td><code>numberOfHours</code></td>
<td><code>numberOfHours</code></td>
<td><code>long</code></td>
<td><code>Long.valueOf()</code> (Default <code>0</code>)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>5</code></td>
<td><code>checkNumber</code></td>
<td><code>checkNumber</code> / <code>checkNumberKey</code></td>
<td><code>String</code></td>
<td>Check number string; also stored in <code>checkNumberKey</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>6</code></td>
<td><code>CheckIssuedDate</code></td>
<td><code>checkDate</code></td>
<td><code>Date</code></td>
<td>Parsed as <code>yyyy-MM-dd</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>7</code></td>
<td><code>payeeOrProvider</code></td>
<td><code>payeeOrProvider</code></td>
<td><code>String</code></td>
<td>Truncated to max <code>50</code> characters in <code>RfrDetailBisToDbProcessor</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>8</code></td>
